      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:88974591e72ec9e159b1bc008a7b2b032cf720000485008800598e575e3fe24b",
      "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002> a field.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a geometric point of <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> denote the absolute Galois group.\nTaking stalks induces an equivalence of categories\n<MATH_0006>\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:fb1b84f5f6367a38f408e0ed89678557fa57fa97cb47a2690947d695f668a749",
      "unit_id": "tag:03QT:statement"
    },
    {
      "chapter": "etale-cohomology",
      "node_kind": "proof",
      "parent_tag": "03QW",
      "placeholders": {
        "ACCENT_0001": "\\'e",
        "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e",
        "MATH_0001": "$G$",
        "MATH_0002": "$M$",
        "MATH_0003": "$X \\to \\Spec(K)$",
        "MATH_0004": "$\\Mor_K(\\Spec(K^{sep}), X)$",
        "MATH_0005": "$M$",
        "MATH_0006": "$G$",
        "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$",
        "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(K)_\\etale$",
        "MATH_0009": "$U \\mapsto \\Mor_K(U, X)$",
        "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}} = \\Mor_K(\\Spec(K^{sep}), X) = M$",
        "MATH_0011": "$G$",
        "REF_0001": "\\ref{pione-lemma-sheaves-point}"
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n",
        "suffix": "\\end{proof}"
      },
      "risk_level": "R3",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:edbf1f580c8410b133e59b5abbac7250bb6305d1d2411f235b75f0c2e9323200",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:be626e1bc0cec4309d0f868b947ec4c11805cfcb6b7fdd3005206cb0ac83d3f4",
      "source_text": "Let us construct the inverse to this functor. In\nFundamental Groups, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe have seen that given a <MATH_0001>-set <MATH_0002> there exists an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004> is\nisomorphic to <MATH_0005> as a <MATH_0006>-set. Consider the sheaf\n<MATH_0007> on <MATH_0008> defined by\nthe rule <MATH_0009>. This is a sheaf as the <ACCENT_0002>tale\ntopology is subcanonical. Then we see that\n<MATH_0010>\nas <MATH_0011>-sets (details omitted). This gives the inverse of the functor and\nwe win.\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a7cce4dbabc12496777cb2310b958ed36406548dba4a8be6ecd73f16bfe44b5",
      "unit_id": "tag:03QT:proof"
    },
    {
