        "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(K)$",
        "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(K)_\\etale$",
        "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}",
        "REF_0002": "\\ref{pione-lemma-sheaves-point}",
        "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-definition-representable-sheaf}"
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-every-sheaf-representable}\n",
        "suffix": "\\end{remark}"
      },
      "risk_level": "R3",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff4484f9db6a69d8020f1ab62d01c8633ed85ff42f05e2be7a80da82864c7e1f",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0faf2c36a36539cd57e311d43f24c551f777d5d768f7d3108cc41418cbcdc73b",
      "source_text": "Another way to state the conclusion of\nTheorem <REF_0001> and\nFundamental Groups, Lemma <REF_0002>\nis to say that every sheaf on <MATH_0001> is representable\nby a scheme <MATH_0002> <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0003>.\nThis does not mean that every sheaf is representable in the sense of\nSites, Definition <REF_0003>.\nThe reason is that in our construction of <MATH_0004>\nwe chose a sufficiently large set of schemes <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0005>,\nwhereas sheaves on <MATH_0006> form a proper class.\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:d1612ca0ce318f3373c31788b159938b617c179141337b784aaa399dbb3f4f34",
      "unit_id": "tag:04JL:statement"
    },
    {
      "chapter": "etale-cohomology",
      "node_kind": "lemma",
      "parent_tag": "03QW",
      "placeholders": {
        "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\Gamma(S, \\mathcal{F}) = (\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}})^G\n$$",
        "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}"
      },
      "render": {
        "prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-global-sections-point}\n",
        "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"
      },
      "risk_level": "R3",
      "schema_version": 1,
      "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
      "source_math_hash": "sha256:d550ecfe3e9af773a459da9dde465f13bdf20f6881a8563f7a2219b684d16e17",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
      "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3bf4f0f72c86c07a305b9348b5352a8b62cd0b85a57aab8f7c494908f104111e",
      "source_text": "Assumptions and notations as in\nTheorem <REF_0001>.\nThere is a functorial bijection\n<MATH_0001>\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:635949cbff170addfa6a073a720d64b0bc65823363c61bfa33bcf98075ef8920",
      "unit_id": "tag:04JM:statement"
